A||||5||87ECO5||Emergency Brake Handle Position Sensor Adjustment||||1||
Z||000000||87ECO5||04-17-2000||01:39 PM||||I'm guessing there's a switch or a sensor or something in the emergency brake handle assembly that illuminates the 'BRAKE' light on the gauge pod when the handle is raised off of the floor (thus activating the rear calipers).<P>Yesterday, I started having a problem where, even when the e-brake handle is completely down against the floor, the light on the gauge pod stays on.  I can wiggle the e-brake handle and get the light to turn off but, if I let go, the handle moves and the light illuminates again.<P>Is there an adjustment that can be made to this assembly or should I start looking at a replacement assembly?<P>TIA||||reg||1
Z||000001||N_Man||04-17-2000||06:15 PM||||You Can adjust the brake cables.  Look under the car behind the rear crossmember, in about the middle of the car.<P>Also check the return spings on the calipers and check to see the cable isn't rusted into the housing.<P>The light and the buzzer come on because of a contact that gets broken at the end of the cable under the leather boot of the emergency brake if for any of the above reasons the cable doesnt release (pull tight)the contact will not form and cause problems.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||william_thorniii||04-17-2000||06:18 PM||||87ec05..<P>uhhhh, 56' did it!  It is definitely all his fault.  He started off in the driver’s seat and I finished up.  When we switched, places, the parking brake was set.  It did not feel like it was actuating properly.  In fact, we noticed the travel on your brake is shorter than it is on any of our cars.  Therefore we concluded that the equalizer must need some attention.  I can't believe this is a new problem.  I am so sorry that it occurred when 56' and I were driving it.  We hoped it was something you were used to dealing with since we did know you had e-brake problems... hence the brick.  We meant to mention it to you but completely forgot in all the excitement.  Seriously though, we did make sure that it was not in fact actuated.  I can't believe we forgot to tell you... sorry.  <P>If it is any conciliation, my coupe has the same problem.  It started when I removed the plastic shroud around the brake.  I used to shove my radio face box in between the handle and the seat, but recently I just pulled the chime and the light has stayed on.  You know how long it takes me to take the time to work on my Coupe.  Perhaps in May we can get together and get this fixed.  <P>Terribly Embarrassed,<P>William T. Thorn, III<BR><p>[This message has been edited by william_thorniii (edited 04-17-2000).]||||reg||2
Z||000003||theogre||04-17-2000||06:33 PM||||the switch is on top of the lever where it can get whacked. just carefully bend the top leaf untill it works right.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||04-17-2000||10:52 PM||||Scott, it was my fault. We were trading places in somebodys driveway and I pulled the handle. Then realized it wasn't working properly. I remembered the light was still on your car when I was at work today, and was planning on letting you know what happened. You will be glad to know, I watched for smoke coming from the rotors while William drove. No smoke from the brakes, but... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">. Just kidding, we were nice to your car.||||reg||1
